1
00:00:00,295 --> 00:00:03,005
(Sheldon:)...to verify the identity
of one's coconspirators.

2
00:00:03,173 --> 00:00:06,513
PENNY: Is that Raj and Howard?
- Possibly, but unverified.

3
00:00:06,676 --> 00:00:08,216
Would you just let us in?

4
00:00:08,387 --> 00:00:11,477
(Sheldon:)Luckily for you,
this is not a nuclear reactor.

5
00:00:11,640 --> 00:00:13,310
So, what'd you get the birthday boy?

6
00:00:13,475 --> 00:00:16,435
(Howard:)Raj got him an awesome
limited-edition Dark Knight sculpture...

7
00:00:16,603 --> 00:00:18,483
(Howard:)...based on Alex Ross'
definitive Batman.

8
00:00:18,647 --> 00:00:22,567
(Howard:)And I got him this amazing autographed
copy of The Feynman Lectures on Physics.

9
00:00:22,734 --> 00:00:26,114
(Penny:)Nice. I got him a sweater.

10
00:00:26,738 --> 00:00:30,448
(Howard:)Okay, well, he might like that.
I've seen him get chilly.

11
00:00:31,243 --> 00:00:34,623
(Penny:)- Sheldon, I didn't see your present.
- That's because I didn't bring one.

12
00:00:34,788 --> 00:00:35,918
(Penny:)- Why not?
- Don't ask.

13
00:00:36,081 --> 00:00:39,121
The entire institution of gift-giving
makes no sense.

14
00:00:39,292 --> 00:00:42,462
- Too late.
- Let's say I go out and I spend $50 on you.

15
00:00:42,629 --> 00:00:45,759
(Sheldon:)It's a laborious activity
because I have to imagine what you need...

16
00:00:45,924 --> 00:00:47,504
...where you know what you need.

17
00:00:47,676 --> 00:00:50,806
I could simplify things,
just give you the $50 directly...

18
00:00:50,971 --> 00:00:53,811
...and then you could give me $50
on my birthday and so on...

19
00:00:53,974 --> 00:01:00,024
(Sheldon:)...until one of us dies,
leaving the other one old and $50 richer.

